1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:09,700
Financial Plan Invest one billion dollars. Pass a treaty. Manage twenty-seven point two billion dollars a year forever.

2
00:00:10,600 --> 00:00:17,400
Eighty percent cures diseases, ten percent pays investors, ten percent keeps politicians obedient.

3
00:00:18,220 --> 00:00:26,720
Three pillars, no committees, no generosity required. Most financial plans are complicated because the writers are confused

4
00:00:26,720 --> 00:00:35,520
or lying. This one is complicated because you're convincing one hundred and ninety-five countries to voluntarily stop buying

5
00:00:35,520 --> 00:00:42,800
so many weapons while paying your investors forever. The architecture is embarrassingly simple.

6
00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:51,740
Raise one billion dollars. Spend it to pass the treaty. Manage twenty-seven point two billion dollars plus annually forever.

7
00:00:53,820 --> 00:01:00,920
Three things. That's the whole financial plan. The rest of this chapter is just explaining why your species needs four thousand

8
00:01:00,920 --> 00:01:07,880
words to understand three things. Pillar One: The Money Part (Raise one billion dollars).

9
00:01:09,120 --> 00:01:17,640
The instrument is a VICTORY Incentive Alignment Bond, which is a piece of paper that says "give us money now, get much more

10
00:01:17,640 --> 00:01:22,400
money later, forever." On Wishonia, this would be called "fraud."

11
00:01:23,000 --> 00:01:27,220
On Earth, it's called "finance." The difference is collateral.

12
00:01:27,880 --> 00:01:31,960
The bonds return two hundred and seventy-two percent annually.

13
00:01:32,760 --> 00:01:39,680
This looks like a typo. It's arithmetic: two point seven two billion dollars divided by one billion dollars.

14
00:01:40,660 --> 00:01:48,220
Senior debt structure, meaning the fund pays bondholders before anyone else, because investors don't care about your moral

15
00:01:48,220 --> 00:01:56,620
framework until after they've been paid. They receive ten percent of all treaty inflows (two point seven two billion dollars

16
00:01:56,620 --> 00:02:01,360
a year), collateralized against the entire military budget of the planet.

17
00:02:02,220 --> 00:02:05,420
Every Ponzi scheme in history has promised returns like this.

18
00:02:06,000 --> 00:02:10,300
The difference is that Bernie Madoff's collateral was a spreadsheet he made up.

19
00:02:11,160 --> 00:02:18,660
Your collateral is twenty-seven point two billion dollars plus in annual treaty revenue, which, unlike Bernie's spreadsheet,

20
00:02:19,140 --> 00:02:23,960
actually exists. You raise one billion dollars in twelve to twenty-four months.

21
00:02:24,620 --> 00:02:30,160
Donations would require generosity. Bonds require greed. Greed is faster.

22
00:02:30,820 --> 00:02:37,600
This is the single most important insight about your species and I've been trying to communicate it for four thousand two

23
00:02:37,600 --> 00:02:46,320
hundred and ninety-seven years. Why one billion dollars? Your opposition spends four hundred and fifty million dollars a

24
00:02:46,320 --> 00:02:54,100
year to keep things exactly as terrible as they are (pharma lobbying at roughly three hundred million dollars a year plus

25
00:02:54,100 --> 00:02:59,080
the military-industrial complex at roughly one hundred and fifty million dollars a year).

26
00:02:59,640 --> 00:03:07,980
A subscription to suffering. You raise one billion dollars ONCE to pass a treaty that generates twenty-seven point two billion

27
00:03:07,980 --> 00:03:17,180
dollars a year FOREVER. Over a ten-year campaign, opposition spends roughly four point five billion dollars to your one

28
00:03:17,180 --> 00:03:24,300
billion dollars. But their four hundred and fifty million dollars a year is spread across thousands of contracts and dozens

29
00:03:24,300 --> 00:03:29,620
of incumbents. Your one billion dollars is aimed at a single treaty.

30
00:03:29,880 --> 00:03:37,900
Concentrated offense beats diffuse defense. This is military strategy, which is ironic, and also the only kind of strategy

31
00:03:37,900 --> 00:03:45,160
your species respects. Nobody gets paid unless it works. Lawyers get success-based compensation.

32
00:03:45,820 --> 00:03:51,100
Team compensation is mostly equity. This is how you know it's not a government program.

33
00:03:51,920 --> 00:03:59,160
The Seed phase requires two hundred and fifty to four hundred million dollars for the platform, policy frameworks, and pilots,

34
00:03:59,520 --> 00:04:05,880
with a milestone of fifty million verified participants and a difficulty level of "Convince a few billionaires".

35
00:04:06,620 --> 00:04:14,020
The Series A phase requires five hundred million to one billion dollars to scale to G Seven nations, with a milestone of

36
00:04:14,020 --> 00:04:20,980
three point five percent global participation (two hundred and eighty million people) and a difficulty level of "Convince

37
00:04:20,980 --> 00:04:28,340
several countries". The Growth phase requires five hundred million to one point one billion dollars for the ratification

38
00:04:28,360 --> 00:04:36,320
push in major powers, with a milestone of the first one billion dollar disbursement and a difficulty level of "Convince

39
00:04:36,320 --> 00:04:42,500
the countries with nukes". Ranges reflect scenario planning (optimistic to pessimistic).

40
00:04:43,120 --> 00:04:50,260
The one billion dollar target is the base case; upper bounds cover contingencies because convincing nuclear powers to behave

41
00:04:50,260 --> 00:04:58,340
rationally occasionally requires overtime. Pillar two: The Spending Part (Spend one billion dollars).

42
00:04:59,120 --> 00:05:06,420
The one-time activation energy to convince eight billion people to marginally reduce their commitment to mutual annihilation.

43
00:05:07,160 --> 00:05:14,440
Detailed line items are available. The Global Referendum category takes two hundred and fifty million dollars for the viral

44
00:05:14,440 --> 00:05:18,960
referral system, two hundred and eighty million votes, and platform development.

45
00:05:19,640 --> 00:05:28,040
The Political Lobbying category takes six hundred and fifty million dollars for A.I.-targeted campaigns (U.S./E.U./G Twenty),

46
00:05:28,640 --> 00:05:33,620
Super PACs, and Military-Industrial Complex, or M.I.C., conversion.

47
00:05:34,360 --> 00:05:42,660
This outspends pharma plus the M.I.C. The Reserve Fund category takes one hundred million dollars for the post-passage transition

48
00:05:42,660 --> 00:05:51,040
and a contingency buffer. The Part That Makes It Cheap. Viral referendum mechanics bring the cost down to twenty cents per

49
00:05:51,040 --> 00:05:58,460
vote at the optimistic lower bound (base case fifty cents to eighty-nine cents), compared to five to fifteen dollars per

50
00:05:58,460 --> 00:06:05,800
voter through traditional channels. Getting someone to click "I prefer not dying" costs less than getting someone to click

51
00:06:05,800 --> 00:06:12,580
"I prefer Pepsi." You also focus on twenty high-impact countries, not all one hundred and ninety-five.

52
00:06:13,000 --> 00:06:17,700
You don't need Liechtenstein's permission. Liechtenstein has thirty-nine thousand people.

53
00:06:18,060 --> 00:06:26,260
That's a concert venue, not a geopolitical obstacle. Timeline is thirty-six to sixty months (optimistic) to one hundred

54
00:06:26,260 --> 00:06:29,850
and twenty plus months (realistic, given that you're humans).

55
00:06:30,480 --> 00:06:37,040
The landmine ban took six years, and that was just agreeing not to hide explosives in the ground, which you'd think wouldn't

56
00:06:37,040 --> 00:06:43,960
require a treaty at all. You're betting on viral referendum mechanics and existing disarmament frameworks.

57
00:06:44,620 --> 00:06:50,540
Also on the assumption that your species wants to survive, which, based on my four thousand two hundred and ninety-seven

58
00:06:50,540 --> 00:06:59,760
years of observation, remains an open question. Pillar three: The Forever Part (Manage twenty-seven point two billion dollars

59
00:06:59,760 --> 00:07:08,680
or more per year). Once the treaty passes, twenty-seven point two billion dollars flows annually from "how to kill people"

60
00:07:08,820 --> 00:07:16,000
budgets into "how to stop people dying" budgets. This is the part where your financial plan stops being a financial plan

61
00:07:16,000 --> 00:07:20,120
and starts being a money volcano that erupts on schedule, forever.

62
00:07:20,780 --> 00:07:24,580
One hundred plus nations contribute one percent of military budgets.

63
00:07:25,360 --> 00:07:33,340
Not because they've had a moral awakening. Because the Incentive Alignment Bond mechanism makes compliance self-enforcing:

64
00:07:33,920 --> 00:07:41,420
politicians in non-compliant countries watch their Public Good Scores drop, voters abandon them, and compliance becomes

65
00:07:41,420 --> 00:07:45,930
the career-optimal choice. You don't need politicians to be good.

66
00:07:46,220 --> 00:07:53,520
You just need them to be selfish in the right direction. How the Money Gets Spent: eighty, ten, ten.

67
00:07:54,580 --> 00:08:02,480
The allocation is automatic. No committees. No debates. No one arguing for six months about font choices on the grant application.

68
00:08:03,000 --> 00:08:09,520
Just math, executing silently, like a competent employee (something most of your governments have never experienced).

69
00:08:10,480 --> 00:08:17,860
Eighty percent of the allocation, or twenty-one point eight billion dollars, goes to Clinical Trials and Platform for patient

70
00:08:17,860 --> 00:08:26,800
subsidies, research, and the platform. Ten percent, totaling two point seven two billion dollars, is for VICTORY Bond Returns

71
00:08:26,980 --> 00:08:35,360
for perpetual investor payments. The final ten percent, another two point seven two billion dollars, goes to I.A.B.

72
00:08:35,620 --> 00:08:38,940
Political Incentives as rewards for supporting legislators.

73
00:08:39,480 --> 00:08:43,419
The twenty percent for bonds and political incentives is untouchable.

74
00:08:44,380 --> 00:08:51,580
Smart contracts distribute both automatically. No human hands involved, which, given your track record with money, is a

75
00:08:51,580 --> 00:08:59,480
feature. On Wishonia, we learned four thousand two hundred and ninety-seven years ago that the best way to handle money

76
00:08:59,480 --> 00:09:05,260
is to never let a person touch it. Your species hasn't learned this yet.

77
00:09:05,340 --> 00:09:12,540
Your species has a thing called an "accountant," which is a person you pay to watch your money, who sometimes takes your

78
00:09:12,540 --> 00:09:19,260
money, so you hire a second person called an "auditor" to watch the first person, and then the auditor takes your money.

79
00:09:19,860 --> 00:09:27,460
The smart contract skips all of this. The remaining eighty percent (twenty-one point eight billion dollars per year) funds

80
00:09:27,460 --> 00:09:33,420
clinical trials and research infrastructure. Wishocracy governs the allocation.

81
00:09:33,440 --> 00:09:41,740
Dynamic Patient Subsidies. Instead of paying researchers to write about diseases, you pay patients to participate in curing

82
00:09:41,740 --> 00:09:45,370
them. Paying the people who are actually sick. What a concept.

83
00:09:46,400 --> 00:09:53,580
Patients organize to grow the treasury, because participating in their own survival is, for once, financially rewarded.

84
00:09:54,240 --> 00:10:00,660
Researchers compete to attract patients instead of competing to write persuasive grant applications, which is a different

85
00:10:00,660 --> 00:10:06,060
skill from doing science, the same way writing a restaurant review is a different skill from cooking.

86
00:10:07,120 --> 00:10:11,580
Insurance companies save money because trials are cheaper than decades of chronic suffering.

87
00:10:12,420 --> 00:10:19,980
Compare that to N.I.H. grants: six months of proposal writing, committees judging the writing, universities skimming forty

88
00:10:19,980 --> 00:10:25,920
percent overhead, and then maybe some science. The Whole Thing on One Line.

89
00:10:26,700 --> 00:10:31,920
Invest one billion dollars. Get two point seven two billion dollars per year.

90
00:10:32,440 --> 00:10:38,380
Forever. Your species spent roughly five billion dollars on a particle accelerator to find a boson.

91
00:10:39,020 --> 00:10:42,400
This costs less and finds a cure for dying.
